<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sriram Chandra Bhanj Deo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1871">1871</a>–<a href="/years/1912">1912</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sriram Chandra Bhanj Deo was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharaja</a> of Mayurbhanj, a princely state in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a>, from 1882 to 1912. A modernising ruler, he built schools, hospitals and a light railway, encouraged the study of local archaeology and leased the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gorumahisani">Gorumahisani</a> iron-ore deposits to the Tata company, whose ore supplied the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steel">steel</a> works at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamshedpur">Jamshedpur</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sriram-chandra-bhanj-deo.jpg" alt="Sriram Chandra Bhanj Deo" width="320" height="323" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Subham9423 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shri_Ramachandra_Bhanja_deo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
